            <ArticleTitle>Response to: Correcting for cell-type effects in DNA methylation studies: reference-based method outperforms latent variable approaches in empirical studies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>25</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s13059-017-1149-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We thank Hattab and colleagues for their correspondence and their investigation of cell-type mixture correction methods in methyl-CG binding domain sequencing. Here, we speculate on why surrogate variable analysis (SVA) performed differently between their two data sets, and poorly in one of them.Please see related Correspondence article: https://genomebiology.biomedcentral.com/articles/10/1186/s13059-017-1148-8 and related Research article: https://genomebiology.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s13059-016-0935-y.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
